  HOW CHROMA FINDS THE BEST MATCHING CHUNKS
  ············································································

  Every chunk above is stored as a vector of 1536 floats.
  When you ask a question, it is embedded into the same space.

  Chroma compares the question vector (Q) against every stored
  chunk vector (C) using a simple dot product:

    cos(Q, C)  =  Q · C
               =  Q[0]×C[0] + Q[1]×C[1] + … + Q[1535]×C[1535]

  Score range:   -1.0  →  opposite meaning  (worst)
                  0.0  →  unrelated
                 +1.0  →  identical meaning  (best match)

  Value range in your vectors:  min = -0.11084   max = +0.11816
  ············································································

